# The spline tour: a serpentine -- four half-circles of alternating
# curvature, driven as arcs.
#
# WHY THIS SHAPE. The elite suite's spline tours (complex_spline.tour,
# tag_spline.tour) follow a fitted SVG path with pure pursuit, and say
# what makes such a path hard: "repeated left/right reversals". This
# repo has no path follower -- SPLINE is one of the directives
# tourfile.py reports as not executed -- so the reversal itself is what
# is worth keeping. A serpentine is exactly that and nothing else: the
# curvature flips sign at every join, with no straight in between to
# let the heading servo settle. Where circle.tour holds one curvature
# and infinity.tour reverses it twice per lap, this reverses it three
# times in a row.
#
# It is NOT a fitted spline and should not be described as one. It is
# the curvature-reversal half of what a spline test measures, which is
# the half this robot can drive.
#
# SIZING. r = 150 mm. Each half circle advances 2r along the axis and
# stays within +-r of it, so four bends span 4 x 2r = 1200 mm by
# 300 mm. Against the +-671.5 x +-446.5 mm centre limit that leaves
# ~71 mm on the long axis (start at x = -600 facing East) and a lot of
# room on the short one. Five bends would span 1500 mm and NOT fit.
#
#   v = omega * r, with omega = 57.3 deg/s = 1.0 rad/s
#   -> v = 1.0 * 150 = 150 mm/s.
#
# SEGMENT SIZE IS NOT FREE. moveX() splits any move with a nonzero
# distance and |rotation| >= 50 deg (kTurnFirstAngleRad) into a pivot
# THEN a straight, so an arc asked for in 90 deg pieces comes out as a
# corner. MEASURED 2026-09-01 on gopiv (reports/tours-20260901/):
# circle.tour written as one 360 deg arc drove a 942 mm STRAIGHT LINE.
# Every arc here is 45 deg, so a half circle is four of them.

SET twist_hold_gain 8
SET speed_floor 512
SET yaw_taper 800
SET pivot_overrun 0.68

# --- bend 1: half circle, CCW ----------------------------------------
MARK bend1
REPEAT 4
TWIST vx=150 omega=57.3 angle=45 timeout=6
END

# --- bend 2: half circle, CW -----------------------------------------
MARK bend2
REPEAT 4
TWIST vx=150 omega=-57.3 angle=-45 timeout=6
END

# --- bend 3: half circle, CCW ----------------------------------------
MARK bend3
REPEAT 4
TWIST vx=150 omega=57.3 angle=45 timeout=6
END

# --- bend 4: half circle, CW -----------------------------------------
MARK bend4
REPEAT 4
TWIST vx=150 omega=-57.3 angle=-45 timeout=6
END

STOP dwell=0.5

# NOTE ON CLOSURE. A serpentine is an OPEN path: it ends 1200 mm from
# where it started, so the closure number run_tour.py prints is
# meaningless here and should be ignored. What this tour scores is the
# heading at the end -- four half circles alternating direction net to
# ZERO net rotation, so a clean run finishes on the starting heading.
# Read `net rotation` in the run output, not `closure`.
